    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Thank you, Sir. Again, I am sorry for being late since it was due to a medical matter that I had to attend to.\n\nI would like to ask the following Question from the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development under Standing Order No. 27(2).\n\nThe Government has projected an export revenue target of US Dollars 19 billion. However, the removal of SVAT without a proper refund system could severely impact on cash flows, discourage exports and create financial uncertainty among exporters, including SMEs. The lack of a swift and transparent refund mechanism may lead to delays, increasing the cost of doing business and affecting the competitiveness of Sri Lankan exports in global markets.\n\nSri Lankan exporters have to compete in a region where all benefits are being given to the competing peer country companies with a very low cost of capital and no administrative hassles. Sir, I raise this is in light of President Trump adopting an anti-globalization approach. So, that is the reason why we have to look at it and help our companies to reach international state.\n\nIn light of all this, I seek a response from the Hon. Minister of Finance on the following:\n\n1. What measures are being taken to ensure a timely and a guaranteed VAT refund system before abolishing SVAT?\n\n2. Evasion of taxes must be eradicated at all cost. However, in order to achieve that, a feeling of equity and reasonableness must be demonstrated. When tax refunds have become a major \"nightmare\", do you think adopting this measure at this stage would be practical? This has been tried for the last seven years.\n\n3. Has the Government consulted key stakeholders, including exporters, the chambers of commerce and the SME chambers on the practical challenges arising from this decision?"
  },
