    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Deputy Minister, I appreciate your very practical answer. That is what I am getting at. You quoted earlier what I had mentioned. We were all thinking that the prospective approach ASYCUDA would be introduced and that it would link up the 34 government institutions. But, Hon. Minister, the situation is that the officials do not work in the speed that you and I would like them to. That is the reason why I said that at that particular moment. That has been an attempt made for about seven or eight years. Tax evasion is there. I know that what you stated is a laudable step, but the point of sale approach that the President addressed in the Budget Speech is what you have got to take forward.\n\nThe other matter is, when you are competing in a region where there is an interest rate of 3 to 4 per cent, our competition basically has a 10 to 11 per cent cost of capital disadvantage.\n\nSir, the other matter is, the Central Bank makes Monetary Policy, but they must follow Government policy as well. You expect Rs. 5 trillion to be your revenue. With an interest rate of 17 to 18 per cent, you would never be able to achieve the expected 5 per cent growth in the economy in the next ten months or by the end of the financial year.\n\nSo, it is in that spirit I raised this Question, being an exporter. Therefore, please ensure that you take a practical approach with regard to this issue, like the Answer you gave. So, I appreciate if the SVAT would be done away with, with only a guaranteed refund system in place.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dba) \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0da2\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dad\u0dca\u200d \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0bc8\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) Thank you very much, Hon. Member.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0d85\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db1 \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0da2\u0dd3\u0dc0 \u0dc3\u0dd9\u0db1\u0db1\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d82\u0dc4 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf \u0b85\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b9c\u0bc1\u0ba9 \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0b9c\u0bc0\u0bb5 \u0ba4\u0b9a\u0ba9\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0b99\u0bcd\u0bb9) (The Hon. Arjuna Sujeewa Senasinghe, Attorney-at-Law) Sir, I just want a clarification regarding a small point. So, may I be permitted -"
  },
  {
