    "chunk_size_bytes": 2386,
    "chunk_text": "Then, regarding ASYCUDA, which you raised about, the point of sale approach and e-invoicing, I would like to say that we have to bring in technology to have a very good system for VAT refund and of course, to go for point of sale machines and e-invoicing. Initial discussions and work has already been done in this regard with consultation of all the stakeholders.\n\nSo, thank you very for your constructive ideas. We will work accordingly.\n\nThank you.\n\n1587 1588\n\n2025 \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 08\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0dba \u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Deputy Minister, are you willing to respond to that?\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0d85\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db1 \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0da2\u0dd3\u0dc0 \u0dc3\u0dd9\u0db1\u0db1\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d82\u0dc4 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf \u0b85\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b9c\u0bc1\u0ba9 \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0b9c\u0bc0\u0bb5 \u0ba4\u0b9a\u0ba9\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0b99\u0bcd\u0bb9) (The Hon. Arjuna Sujeewa Senasinghe, Attorney-at-Law) This is just a small clarification on the same matter. Hon. Deputy Minister, you said that a directive cannot be given by the Central Bank on interest rates and other decisions made by the banks. The Governor of the Central Bank also said that they cannot -\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0db8\u0dc4\u0dcf\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dba) \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0da2\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dad\u0dca\u200d \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0ba4\u0baa\u0bb0\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0bc8\u0bb0\u0bcd) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0bc8\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) A directive cannot be given, but there are lacunas in the monitoring system. Of course, the Central Bank is authorized to direct the banks and the financial institutions. They are doing it. We know that this is not something that happens all of a sudden. This has been observed in the past or during the previous times as well. So, it is being monitored gradually, Hon. Member. You know that there is a time lag involved. When these statutory rates and the policy rates are announced, the banks may not adjust accordingly. Of course, the State banks may adjust, but other banks may not. So, to some extent, the Central Bank can do that. On the other hand, we strongly believe that a proper market mechanism, demand for money, supply and the revival of economic activities would do the rest. So, it has to go parallelly or hand in hand, I believe."
  },
