    "chunk_size_bytes": 2027,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Chairman) The Hon. Faiszer Musthapha. You have 17 minutes. [1.09 p.m.] \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dc6\u0dba\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad \u0dd4\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0ba9\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf \u0bae\u0baa\u0bb8\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bc1\u0bb8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe) (The Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, PC) Hon. Chairman, I am thankful to you for giving me the opportunity to speak at the Committee Stage Discussion on the Votes of the Ministry of Women and Child Affairs. Today is also the International Women\u2019s Day.\n\nBut, unfortunately, Hon. Minister, we have a male-chauvinistic society. We have a 52 per cent women population, but how many of our women are part of our workforce is a question. There is an issue which I would like to raise with regard to Muslim women in this country. As you are aware, the Muslim Marriage and Divorce Act was brought about in 1951. The community has been agitating with regard to certain reforms. There have been various committees, various meetings. We, as Muslim politicians, also should be held responsible for not bringing in certain amendments that should have been brought in. Hon. Minister, you are aware of it. Also as you are aware, in terms of the general Marriage Registration Ordinance, the age of marriage is 18. The Muslims, as a community, are at a consensus that it should be 18. So, Hon. Minister, I do not think there is any impediment for you to bring in that reform and for exceptional circumstances, there should be a proviso. In addition, if you take the Muslim women\u2019s right to sign the marriage certificate or give consent, we should bring in\n\nreform to provide for a Muslim woman, at the time of marriage, to sign the marriage certificate. That is an urgent reform needed and I do not think you need to wait any longer because there is a consensus among the community to do that."
  },
