    "md5": "9c5a6c335a8c658f3de4a1df7aaca309",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 826,
    "chunk_text": "reform to provide for a Muslim woman, at the time of marriage, to sign the marriage certificate. That is an urgent reform needed and I do not think you need to wait any longer because there is a consensus among the community to do that.\n\nIn addition, if you take maintenance, it is adjudicated in the Magistrate\u2019s Court. But, if a Muslim woman wants to get maintenance, she first has to go to the Quazi Court, get an order and then get it enforced by the Magistrate\u2019s Court. So, I would suggest that you make provision for a direct mechanism, through which a Muslim woman also can go direct to the Magistrate\u2019s Court and seek maintenance.\n\nHon. Minister, with regard to the Judiciary, I have to bring up an issue, which does not come under your Ministerial Consultative Committee, but is a matter of national importance."
  },
