    "md5": "4d3e28d122c3be1ebbe3336828ca8fc8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1349,
    "chunk_text": "That is justly due. And, I believe that the estate women are the most affected. I started my politics from the Ceylon Workers\u2019 Congress. Therefore, the estate worker is always a subject which I would touch upon.\n\nthe Prevention of Domestic Violence Act, if a woman is abused or threatened, she can go to the Magistrate\u2019s Court and get a restraining order. But, unfortunately, women are not aware of it. It is a very simple mechanism, but a very powerful tool. You can get a restraining order to prevent the man who purports violence against his wife from even coming home. Therefore, please look at it because that is a very important aspect.\n\nThen, let us look at women who go overseas for employment. Unfortunately, the majority of the women go as housemaids and they are unskilled workers or skilled at a lower level. We need to promote more skilled women leaving the country for employment overseas. When women go as housemaids, there is a grave social cost and that also should be looked into. We should try to discourage women who have young children from going overseas as housemaids by giving them income-earning opportunities in Sri Lanka and empowering them. I believe a lot of self-employment programmes have been initiated and thereby, a lot of women who thought they need to go abroad have opted otherwise, not to leave the country."
  },
  {
