    "num": "2025-03-08",
    "date_str": "2025-03-08",
    "description": "Hansard of March 08, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1743142289059261.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-03-08-2025-03-08-0103",
    "chunk_index": 103,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "a61526cb702ded52d93a6f2396a0c0ba",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1714,
    "chunk_text": "Then, let us look at women who go overseas for employment. Unfortunately, the majority of the women go as housemaids and they are unskilled workers or skilled at a lower level. We need to promote more skilled women leaving the country for employment overseas. When women go as housemaids, there is a grave social cost and that also should be looked into. We should try to discourage women who have young children from going overseas as housemaids by giving them income-earning opportunities in Sri Lanka and empowering them. I believe a lot of self-employment programmes have been initiated and thereby, a lot of women who thought they need to go abroad have opted otherwise, not to leave the country.\n\nIn addition, if you take children in this country, child abuse takes place at a greater rate, against which we need to bring in a mechanism. Generally, if you take schools, there are instances where teachers have sexually harassed children.\n\nBut, a child is not aware what sexually harassed means. So, they should include it in the school curriculum and every school should conduct programmes to explain children that if anybody sexually harasses them, the law would take care of them. In addition, in schools, there should be a mechanism where there is a special, dedicated person - either the principal or a special person assigned - to whom any child, who is sexually harassed by their school teacher or by any other teacher, could go and complain because sexual harassment of children is on the rise. So, that also has to be looked at very seriously.\n\n1631 1632\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dba\u0dba\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0dbb\u0dca \u0dd4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad \u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 08"
  },
  {
