    "chunk_text": "nothing compared to the amount of effort they make and the goodwill they repose in those students. It is actually nothing! And, it is in that respect I would ask the Hon. Prime Minister to see my comments.\n\nSo, if we take the increments that are being offered under this Budget for the next three years and the whole of what was recommended by the Subodhini Salary Commission for three years, had it been fully implemented - it was implemented only in the first year - an SLTS 2-II teacher would get, under this Budget, a salary of Rs. 66,880 whereas under the Subodhini Salary Commission Recommendations, she would have got Rs. 82,150, a difference of Rs. 15,270. That difference for the grade SLTS 2-I, after the full implementation of the salary increment under this Budget at the end of the next three years and the Subodhini Committee Recommendations at the end of the three years it recommended, would have been Rs. 27,310. So, like that, it goes on. That difference in salary for SLTS 1 would have been Rs. 34,990, for the Sri Lanka Principals' Service - SLPS 3 - Rs. 9,870, for SLPS 2, Rs. 25,120 and for SLPS 1, Rs. 32,230. So, what I am saying is, if the Hon. Prime Minister - if the economy improves in some way - goes to these Subodhini Commission's Recommendations at least in the next Budget, I would be its strongest supporter and can assure the Hon. Prime Minister that not a single Member in this House would oppose her implementing them. There are so many Ministries, totally unnecessary ones, from the Votes of which cuts can be made. One such ministry is the Defence Ministry. But, education is one field, I think, to which we all owe. We all owe those people who work so hard and are so magnanimous in the way they approach this field."
  },
