    "chunk_text": "The Northern Province is in dire need of funds to complete the buildings which have already been started. I have been informed by the Northern Provincial Council that a minimum of Rs. 2 billion is required in order to ensure that the projects that have been started - the construction of those buildings - could, to some extent, be completed. So, that, too, I would ask the Hon. Prime Minister to look into.\n\nSir, I wish to raise one other matter. I brought this matter to your notice earlier also. The UGC has called for examinations for the promotion of Management Assistant Grade III to Grade II and the examination is supposed to be held on the 21st of March. There are 61 applicants from Jaffna. I have been in touch with the Jaffna University. They have written to the UGC and asked - in the previous years when those examinations were held, they were held in Jaffna - that if in case the UGC does not want to hold it on Jaffna, whether it could, at least, be held in Vavuniya because out of the 61 applicants, 40 applicants are females who are either pregnant, feeding mothers or are going through fertility treatment. So, they have asked for special treatment and I do not think it is unreasonable considering the number who are actually willing to sit for this exam. Also, the outside district applicants are also willing to travel to Jaffna; they prefer coming to Jaffna because it is much cheaper and the University says that they will make accommodation possible for them. So, I think the University Grants Commission must consider this request also favourably.\n\n1853 1854\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc1\u0db4\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0dda\u0db6\u0dbd\u0dda \u0db8 \u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dae\u0dd4 10"
